op: Intl.PluralRules.prototype.select
in: str:"en" f64:0x3FF010624DD2F1AA
out: value: str:"one"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row P1: `select` over FormatNumericToString's string: en `{minimumFractionDigits: 1}` 1; de the same ...; Broiler.JS answers selects over the double; the digit options are snapshotted and never applied: `"one"`, `"one"`, `"other"`, `"other"`, `"one"`, `"one"` ...; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0082, C1); answered by SJL-9.5, this engine's cut-over to the shared Intl library
prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-resolveplural spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-formatnumerictostring spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-pluralruleselect ref:intlref@1
script: new Intl.PluralRules("en", {notation: "compact"}).select($f64(0x3ff01062, 0x4dd2f1aa))
note: row P1: ResolvePlural selects over FormatNumericToString's string, with the digit options
since: 27

id: intl/values-and-plurals/plurals/0015
area: intl
op: Intl.PluralRules.prototype.select
in: str:"en"
out: value: str:"one"
class: divergence
divergence.broiler-js: row P2: `select` and `selectRange` of a BigInt: en `1n`, `2n`, `0n`, `-1n`; ordinal `2n`, `3n` ...; Broiler.JS answers `TypeError: Cannot mix BigInt and other types` in every case; a correction of Broiler.JS (JSD-0082, C1); answered by SJL-9.5, this engine's cut-over to the shared Intl library
prov: spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-intl.pluralrules.prototype.select spec:ecma402@3d4c558#sec-tointlmathematicalvalue overruled:intlref@1=error:TypeError
script: new Intl.PluralRules("en", {}).select(1n)
note: row P2: select reads ToIntlMathematicalValue, so a BigInt is a value; the pinned text's select and selectRange read ToIntlMathematicalValue, which takes a BigInt as its mathematical value, and ResolvePlural selects over its formatted digits; the category is the one the reference gives for the same value as a Number (the reference answered error: TypeError)
since: 27

